              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Portuguese for the tow truck, then the Portuguese for the repair garage."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: o capô",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "o capô — \"the bonnet (of a car)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "O mecânico abriu o capô para ver o motor. The mechanic opened the bonnet to check the engine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In Brazil also o capô; in the US, the hood."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "capô was borrowed from French capot 'bonnet, cover' (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
